{
 "about": "Heard-route fixtures for design 12.3, 4.2 and 12.7. Each scenario starts empty: its segments are forecast claims the server wrote (stretch fx) with the text named in `texts`; its batches are sent in order. `results` is the code (and reason of a refusal) per event, in the batch's own order; `settlements` is the segment's settlement ('yes' or 'no') after all batches, absent when none. `pre.air_without_settlement` is events already stored whose settlement was never written. Reason tokens are defined by these fixtures. A segment has `blocks` from its text by SplitBlocks.",
 "texts": {
  "one": {
   "text": "Only one paragraph here.",
